[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":202},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":200,"_13":200,"_29":201},"id","eg","nome","CLL / EG","nomeLongo","Layer and CLL, or face and EG","termo",{"_29":197,"_198":199},"niveis",[147,50],"introducao","<p>For those who already use <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a> and want to go faster. In <a href=\"/en/glossary#cll-eg\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Fast 2x2 methods. In CLL, with the first layer done, the top one takes a single algorithm. In EG only the first face is needed (the bottom…\">CLL</a>, build the whole bottom layer and solve the top one in one go (40 cases). In EG, the bottom face is enough: the algorithm solves the top layer and fixes the bottom one at the same time (80 more cases, EG-1 and EG-2).</p>\n","etapas",[33,34,35],"historias",[27],{"_13":28,"_29":30,"_31":32},"CLL and EG","endereco","/historia#cll-eg","resumo","CLL (solving the top layer at once with the bottom one done) had been discussed since 2003; the first site with algorithms made for the 2x2 was Erik Akkersdijk's, in 2006.",{"_11":190,"_13":191,"_37":192,"_39":193,"_41":194,"_42":-7,"_44":195},{"_11":141,"_13":142,"_37":143,"_39":144,"_41":-7,"_42":145,"_44":45},{"_11":12,"_13":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":-7,"_42":43,"_44":45},"EG-1 and EG-2","html","<p>The method of the fastest solvers: just the bottom face and the rest at once. That&#39;s 80 more cases (<a href=\"/en/glossary#cll-eg\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Fast 2x2 methods. In CLL, with the first layer done, the top one takes a single algorithm. In EG only the first face is needed (the bottom…\">CLL</a> is &quot;EG-0&quot;). Start with EG-1.</p>\n","grupos",[46,47],"pagina","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=eg-1,eg-2","imagem","/imagens/diagramas/02b6a512b5070e6c.svg",{"_11":98,"_13":98,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":99,"_29":100},{"_11":48,"_13":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":56,"_29":57},"EG-2","nivel","avancado","casos",40,"conjunto",false,"ids",[58,59,60,61,62,63,64,65,66,67,68,69,70,71,72,73,74,75,76,77,78,79,80,81,82,83,84,85,86,87,88,89,90,91,92,93,94,95,96,97],"/2x2/eg-2","2X2-EG2AS1","2X2-EG2AS2","2X2-EG2AS3","2X2-EG2AS4","2X2-EG2AS5","2X2-EG2AS6","2X2-EG2H1","2X2-EG2H2","2X2-EG2H3","2X2-EG2H4","2X2-EG2L1","2X2-EG2L2","2X2-EG2L3","2X2-EG2L4","2X2-EG2L5","2X2-EG2L6","2X2-EG2Pi1","2X2-EG2Pi2","2X2-EG2Pi3","2X2-EG2Pi4","2X2-EG2Pi5","2X2-EG2Pi6","2X2-EG2S1","2X2-EG2S2","2X2-EG2S3","2X2-EG2S4","2X2-EG2S5","2X2-EG2S6","2X2-EG2T1","2X2-EG2T2","2X2-EG2T3","2X2-EG2T4","2X2-EG2T5","2X2-EG2T6","2X2-EG2U1","2X2-EG2U2","2X2-EG2U3","2X2-EG2U4","2X2-EG2U5","2X2-EG2U6","EG-1",[101,102,103,104,105,106,107,108,109,110,111,112,113,114,115,116,117,118,119,120,121,122,123,124,125,126,127,128,129,130,131,132,133,134,135,136,137,138,139,140],"/2x2/eg-1","2X2-EG1AS1","2X2-EG1AS2","2X2-EG1AS3","2X2-EG1AS4","2X2-EG1AS5","2X2-EG1AS6","2X2-EG1H1","2X2-EG1H2","2X2-EG1H3","2X2-EG1H4","2X2-EG1L1","2X2-EG1L2","2X2-EG1L3","2X2-EG1L4","2X2-EG1L5","2X2-EG1L6","2X2-EG1Pi1","2X2-EG1Pi2","2X2-EG1Pi3","2X2-EG1Pi4","2X2-EG1Pi5","2X2-EG1Pi6","2X2-EG1S1","2X2-EG1S2","2X2-EG1S3","2X2-EG1S4","2X2-EG1S5","2X2-EG1S6","2X2-EG1T1","2X2-EG1T2","2X2-EG1T3","2X2-EG1T4","2X2-EG1T5","2X2-EG1T6","2X2-EG1U1","2X2-EG1U2","2X2-EG1U3","2X2-EG1U4","2X2-EG1U5","2X2-EG1U6","cll","CLL","<p>With the whole 1st layer done, solve the top one at once (40 cases). Go by the groups with the same orientation (the <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a> shapes).</p>\n",[146],"/2x2/treino?grupo=cll",{"_11":142,"_13":142,"_49":147,"_51":52,"_53":54,"_55":148,"_29":149},"intermediario",[150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189],"/2x2/cll","2X2-CLLAS1","2X2-CLLAS2","2X2-CLLAS3","2X2-CLLAS4","2X2-CLLAS5","2X2-CLLAS6","2X2-CLLH1","2X2-CLLH2","2X2-CLLH3","2X2-CLLH4","2X2-CLLL1","2X2-CLLL2","2X2-CLLL3","2X2-CLLL4","2X2-CLLL5","2X2-CLLL6","2X2-CLLPi1","2X2-CLLPi2","2X2-CLLPi3","2X2-CLLPi4","2X2-CLLPi5","2X2-CLLPi6","2X2-CLLSune1","2X2-CLLSune2","2X2-CLLSune3","2X2-CLLSune4","2X2-CLLSune5","2X2-CLLSune6","2X2-CLLT1","2X2-CLLT2","2X2-CLLT3","2X2-CLLT4","2X2-CLLT5","2X2-CLLT6","2X2-CLLU1","2X2-CLLU2","2X2-CLLU3","2X2-CLLU4","2X2-CLLU5","2X2-CLLU6","primeira-face","1st face","<p>The same face as in <a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a>. For <a href=\"/en/glossary#cll-eg\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Fast 2x2 methods. In CLL, with the first layer done, the top one takes a single algorithm. In EG only the first face is needed (the bottom…\">CLL</a>, the whole layer (the bottom sides matching); for EG, just the face, and the case changes depending on the bottom corners.</p>\n",[],{"_13":191,"_29":196},"/imagens/diagramas/9e280cd467752f31.svg","/2x2/primeira-face","/en/glossary#cll-eg","dica","Fast 2x2 methods. In CLL, with the first layer done, the top one takes a single algorithm. In EG only the first face is needed (the bottom…","2x2","/2x2/",{"_203":204,"_205":206},"cubos",[209,210,211,212,213,214,215],"idiomas",[207,208],"pt","en",{"_11":224,"_13":224},{"_11":200,"_13":200},{"_11":223,"_13":223},{"_11":222,"_13":222},{"_11":220,"_13":221},{"_11":218,"_13":219},{"_11":216,"_13":217},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
